      "sourceTextSha256": "8823c48a878036bc4438f7a7509ad128474fa2f8d9eb6517f19afbe7df01dbce",
      "text": "An early walk on the Liana Chica trail to Sacha’s canopy walkway, a free-standing suspension bridge 36 m high and 275 m long, one of only a few in the world, for a bird’s-eye view of the rainforest; continue on the Liana Grande and Higuerón trails through terra firme and flooded forest among giant kapok and fig trees, learning about medicinal plants. In the afternoon, a walk along the Napo or the Leoncillo trail, in search of black spider monkeys. (B, L, D)",
